From 06b4e6019794104bb9e0272478fc0c37aa6abd86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sohnyj <271139641+sohnyj@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:43:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter: add cropdetect_vulkan filter

Vulkan port of the black mode of cropdetect. A compute shader sums up
the luma plane per row and per column, and the borders are then searched
on the CPU with the logic of vf_cropdetect.c, so that the metadata and
the log output match those of the software filter.

The sums are copied to host-cached memory, if the device has any, before
the CPU reads them, as reads from device memory are uncached on discrete
GPUs.

The samples are read as integers and shifted down to their code values,
and the sums are bounded by the frame size, as the images of hardware
decoders may be larger than the frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
